{{- /* ~/.ssh/allowed_signers — the principals that may sign a git commit.

`gpg.ssh.allowedSignersFile` in ~/.gitconfig points here. Without this file
`git log --show-signature` gives U for each commit, because git cannot name the
signer. The signature is correct, and only the local name check is absent.

git matches the signer against the committer address, and the install profile
decides that address, so the two addresses are both principals.

`namespaces="git"` keeps the key to git signatures. A signature for a different
namespace does not verify with this line.

The key material is not in this repository. `output` reads the public key of
this machine at each `chezmoi apply`, so each machine uses its own key. The file
stays empty until the key is there. */ -}}
{{- $pub := joinPath .chezmoi.homeDir ".ssh/id_ed25519.pub" -}}
{{- if stat $pub -}}
{{- $key := output "cat" $pub | trim | splitList " " -}}
{{ .gitemail }},{{ .gitemailRestricted }} namespaces="git" {{ index $key 0 }} {{ index $key 1 }}
{{- end }}
